{"id": "landlord-and-contractor-same-people", "title": "Three City landlords’ notices carry a City contractor’s telephone, suite or names", "seconds": 144.1, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "85f977a02f1f4c90", "words": 419, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "A lease and a service contract are separate dealings with the City, on separate files.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.12, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["A lease", "approved on its own file"], "b": ["A service contract", "approved on another"], "kicker": "Two dealings with the City"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.42, 0.5, 0.57, 0.92, 1.37, 1.5, 1.84, 2.16, 2.28, 2.4, 2.89, 2.97, 3.36]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "form", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "But each notice lists a telephone, an address, officers and owners.", "t0": 4.24, "t1": 8.15, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Contract notice", "rows": [["Telephone", ""], ["Address", ""], ["Officers and owners", ""]], "sub": "filed for each counterparty"}, "emph": ["officers and owners"], "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.29, 0.66, 0.9, 1.02, 1.72, 1.83, 2.69, 3.2, 3.36]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine"], "text": "So what if a City landlord’s notice carries a City contractor’s details?", "t0": 8.27, "t1": 11.89, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Three City landlords", "sub": "a City contractor’s suite, telephone or names"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.4, 0.57, 0.64, 0.84, 1.31, 1.64, 1.97, 2.04, 2.25, 2.87]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 11.89, "t1": 13.78, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.04, 0.33, 0.44, 0.59, 1.09, 1.27, 1.36]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount"], "text": "Three landlords like that:", "t0": 13.9, "t1": 15.31, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$10,545,447", "label": "paid to three such landlords since fiscal 2019"}, "emph": ["Three"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.64, 0.84]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount"], "text": "10,545,447 dollars since fiscal 2019.", "t0": 15.31, "t1": 18.5, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$10,545,447", "label": "paid to three such landlords since fiscal 2019"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.3, 0.44, 0.69, 0.85, 1.33, 1.84, 2.1, 2.37, 2.66]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "First: 1601 Quesada Avenue.", "t0": 19.12, "t1": 22.06, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "1601 Quesada Avenue", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "a ten-year master lease, 2019", "chip": "$217,200 a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.53, 1.53, 2.0, 2.52]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "The homelessness department rents it from Jelani Inc, at 217,200 dollars a year.", "t0": 22.18, "t1": 27.52, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "1601 Quesada Avenue", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "a ten-year master lease, 2019", "chip": "$217,200 a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.58, 1.03, 1.24, 1.36, 1.5, 1.9, 2.44, 2.57, 2.7, 2.98, 3.44, 3.87, 4.09, 4.32, 4.73, 4.85]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Jelani’s notice gives the same suite as the Bayview Hunters Point Foundation, and two identically named officers.", "t0": 27.64, "t1": 33.01, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Jelani Inc", "sub": "landlord"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "150 Executive Park Blvd #2800", "sub": "the same suite"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Bayview Hunters Point Foundation", "sub": "City contractor"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.4, 0.65, 0.79, 0.93, 1.16, 1.53, 1.64, 1.76, 2.07, 2.39, 2.61, 3.44, 3.56, 3.82, 4.4, 4.7]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[2]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "The foundation’s own tax returns list Jelani as a related organization, which it controls.", "t0": 33.13, "t1": 37.89, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "irs", "kicker": "The foundation’s tax returns", "text": "list Jelani Inc as a related organization, with the foundation as its controlling entity", "mark": "controlling entity"}, "emph": ["controls"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.59, 0.8, 1.06, 1.54, 1.84, 2.23, 2.3, 2.38, 2.73, 3.76, 3.91, 4.07]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[2]"], "text": "Since fiscal 2019, the foundation got 106.5 million dollars.", "t0": 38.01, "t1": 42.79, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Bayview Hunters Point Foundation", "$106,549,191"], "b": ["Jelani Inc", "$1,612,882"], "kicker": "Paid since fiscal 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.49, 0.76, 1.47, 1.56, 2.03, 2.23, 2.42, 2.73, 3.05, 3.42, 3.65, 4.18]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[2]"], "text": "Its related company, 1,612,882.", "t0": 42.91, "t1": 45.53, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Bayview Hunters Point Foundation", "$106,549,191"], "b": ["Jelani Inc", "$1,612,882"], "kicker": "Paid since fiscal 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 1.0, 1.26, 1.4, 1.69, 1.95]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "story[3]"], "text": "Second, a hotel. From May 2020, the City booked the Adante Hotel as shelter.", "t0": 45.75, "t1": 51.22, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Adante Hotel", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "shelter rooms from May 14, 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.63, 0.73, 1.34, 2.25, 2.44, 2.7, 3.28, 3.38, 3.64, 3.88, 3.98, 4.4, 4.8, 4.98]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["story[3]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The hotel’s payee got 20,215,736 dollars.", "t0": 51.34, "t1": 54.64, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$20,215,736", "label": "paid to the payee Adante Hotel since fiscal 2019", "sub": "booking ceiling: $20,870,507"}, "emph": ["The"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.58, 1.0, 1.23, 1.45, 1.78, 2.07, 2.32, 2.73]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "The booking ended on March 31, 2025. The next day, a lease of the same hotel began.", "t0": 55.16, "t1": 60.78, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2025-03-31", "to": "2025-04-01", "days": "1", "fromLab": "booking ends", "toLab": "lease begins", "kicker": "The Adante Hotel"}, "emph": ["The next day"], "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.34, 0.6, 0.74, 0.99, 1.79, 1.99, 2.86, 3.41, 3.69, 4.03, 4.14, 4.38, 4.44, 4.55, 4.82, 5.16]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[3]"], "text": "The new landlord: Roshan Investments LLC,", "t0": 60.9, "t1": 63.73, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Roshan Investments LLC", "kicker": "The new landlord", "sub": "93 units, file 250194", "chip": "$1,484,280 a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.32, 1.17, 1.58, 2.22]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[3]"], "text": "at 1,484,280 dollars a year for 93 units.", "t0": 63.73, "t1": 67.71, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Roshan Investments LLC", "kicker": "The new landlord", "sub": "93 units, file 250194", "chip": "$1,484,280 a year"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.34, 0.56, 0.76, 1.08, 1.3, 1.75, 2.07, 2.16, 2.44, 2.69, 3.32]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[3]"], "text": "The Board approved the lease retroactively, after it had begun. The records don't say why.", "t0": 67.83, "t1": 72.91, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "approved retroactively", "kicker": "Board file 250194"}, "emph": ["retroactively"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.25, 0.56, 0.65, 0.94, 2.05, 2.32, 2.43, 2.54, 3.09, 3.58, 3.91, 4.11, 4.29]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The hotel’s notices and the landlord’s give the same telephone, and three identically named officers or owners.", "t0": 73.03, "t1": 78.71, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Adante Hotel notices", "the same telephone"], "b": ["Roshan Investments LLC notices", "3 names alike"], "kicker": "Operator and landlord"}, "emph": ["the same telephone"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.54, 1.1, 1.22, 1.32, 1.83, 1.97, 2.11, 2.31, 3.23, 3.37, 3.59, 4.11, 4.39, 4.84, 5.01]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "The records don’t show whether these are the same people, or different people with the same names.", "t0": 78.83, "t1": 82.71, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The same owners?", "sub": "unknown whether the same people or different people"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.63, 0.76, 0.96, 1.08, 1.17, 1.32, 1.58, 2.04, 2.3, 2.64, 2.89, 3.02, 3.12, 3.41]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[4]"], "text": "Third, and weakest: RACHRIS LLC, the Human Services Agency’s landlord at 2 Gough Street.", "t0": 82.93, "t1": 88.52, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "2 Gough Street", "kicker": "The third lead, and the weakest", "sub": "Human Services Agency offices", "chip": "$624,116 a year from July 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.53, 1.3, 2.07, 2.62, 2.91, 3.18, 3.59, 4.06, 4.58, 4.73, 4.97, 5.24]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[4]"], "text": "Its notices give the telephone of Celerity Consulting Group, a City Attorney contractor.", "t0": 88.64, "t1": 93.05, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "RACHRIS, LLC", "sub": "landlord, 2 Gough Street"}, {"art": "question", "name": "the same telephone", "sub": "1 name alike"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Celerity Consulting Group", "sub": "litigation support, City Attorney"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.63, 0.75, 0.84, 1.22, 1.33, 1.78, 2.26, 3.0, 3.11, 3.3, 3.65]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[4]", "established[7]"], "text": "Celerity’s own notice gives its address: 2 Gough Street. The landlord’s email is at consultcelerity.com.", "t0": 93.17, "t1": 99.51, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "kicker": "Celerity’s own notice", "text": "gives 2 Gough Street as its address", "mark": "2 Gough Street"}, "emph": ["2 Gough Street"], "wt": [0.0, 0.51, 0.71, 1.03, 1.23, 1.38, 2.13, 2.4, 2.71, 3.21, 3.71, 4.18, 4.51, 4.66, 4.85]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "story[5]"], "text": "Then the payment file.", "t0": 99.73, "t1": 100.63, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Celerity Consulting Group", "kicker": "The payment file", "sub": "who paid it?", "chip": "$1,336,517 since fiscal 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.14, 0.5]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "story[5]"], "text": "Celerity was paid 1,336,517 dollars. By whom?", "t0": 100.75, "t1": 104.63, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Celerity Consulting Group", "kicker": "The payment file", "sub": "who paid it?", "chip": "$1,336,517 since fiscal 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.5, 0.63, 0.78, 1.03, 1.19, 1.48, 1.58, 1.92, 2.73, 3.07]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[5]"], "text": "1,336,067 came from the Human Services Agency, the tenant.", "t0": 104.63, "t1": 108.6, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Human Services Agency, FY2019 to 2021", "$1,336,067"], "b": ["City Attorney", "$450"], "kicker": "Who paid Celerity"}, "emph": ["the tenant"], "wt": [0.04, 0.49, 0.65, 0.95, 1.1, 1.43, 1.63, 1.81, 1.9, 2.17, 2.66, 3.41, 3.51]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[5]"], "text": "The City Attorney paid 450.", "t0": 108.72, "t1": 110.63, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Human Services Agency, FY2019 to 2021", "$1,336,067"], "b": ["City Attorney", "$450"], "kicker": "Who paid Celerity"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.23, 0.64, 0.89, 1.07, 1.33]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[5]"], "text": "Then the agency’s payments to RACHRIS begin:", "t0": 110.75, "t1": 113.12, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$7,448,285", "label": "paid to RACHRIS LLC from fiscal 2020"}, "emph": ["Then"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.22, 0.67, 1.01, 1.13, 1.56]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[5]"], "text": "7,448,285 dollars.", "t0": 113.12, "t1": 115.4, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$7,448,285", "label": "paid to RACHRIS LLC from fiscal 2020"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.6, 0.96, 1.13, 1.67]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[6]", "story[5]"], "text": "What were Celerity’s payments for? The voucher file answers:", "t0": 115.92, "t1": 119.56, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "e23h", "kicker": "The voucher file", "text": "books $1,330,928 of the agency’s payments to Celerity as property rent for 2 Gough Street", "mark": "property rent"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.19, 0.74, 1.16, 1.64, 2.14, 2.48, 2.75]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[6]", "story[5]"], "text": "rent for 2 Gough Street, 1,330,928 dollars.", "t0": 119.56, "t1": 123.36, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "e23h", "kicker": "The voucher file", "text": "books $1,330,928 of the agency’s payments to Celerity as property rent for 2 Gough Street", "mark": "property rent"}, "emph": ["rent"], "wt": [0.04, 0.42, 0.59, 0.85, 1.17, 1.84, 2.15, 2.31, 2.6, 2.71, 3.19]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[5]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The rent went to the firm, then to the landlord company. The records don’t say why.", "t0": 123.88, "t1": 128.44, "shot": "b24b", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Celerity Consulting Group", "sub": "rent, fiscal 2019 and 2020"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "RACHRIS LLC", "sub": "rent, from fiscal 2020"}], "kicker": "Who took the rent for 2 Gough Street"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.31, 0.46, 0.56, 0.69, 1.19, 1.37, 1.43, 1.53, 2.0, 2.68, 2.93, 3.31, 3.53, 3.78]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["story[6]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Each arrangement is common in property. No wrongdoing is shown.", "t0": 128.66, "t1": 131.8, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any lease was mispriced", "Whether the Board was told", "Whether the names are the same people"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.51, 0.64, 0.89, 0.99, 1.62, 1.98, 2.47, 2.66]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The lease files, and State filings on who owns each landlord.", "t0": 131.92, "t1": 136.52, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The Real Estate Division’s three lease files"}, {"who": "", "what": "Secretary of State filings for each landlord"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.31, 0.6, 0.93, 1.38, 1.68, 2.23, 2.58, 2.85, 3.24, 3.38, 3.59, 3.84, 4.06]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "One tie is confirmed by the foundation’s own returns. No authority has made a finding.", "t0": 136.64, "t1": 140.6, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.33, 0.46, 0.8, 0.91, 1.0, 1.52, 1.69, 2.38, 2.74, 3.19, 3.32, 3.46, 3.54]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 140.72, "t1": 143.18, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.36, 0.49, 0.57, 1.38, 1.63, 1.78]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Two dealings", "lead1": "Lead 1 · 1601 Quesada", "lead2": "Lead 2 · the Adante Hotel", "lead3": "Lead 3 · 2 Gough Street", "lead4": "Lead 4 · who paid Celerity", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "contrast"}